#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# exponent

#% text
# `exponent(e, x)` gives the largest power of x in the expanded form of e.

#% text
# `exponent(e, x, h)` applies h to the list of all the powers: `min` gives the smallest, `list` all of them.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Powers may be rational or symbolic; the exponent of 0 is `-inf`. x may be any expression, such as `cos(x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
exponent(1 + x^2 + a*x^3, x)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
exponent((x^2 + 1)^3 - 1, x, min)
#% output
#= 2

#% cell
exponent(1 + x^2 + a*x^3, x, list)
#% output
#= [0, 2, 3]

#% cell
exponent(x^(k + 1) + 2*sqrt(x) + 1, x)
#% output
#= max(1/2, 1 + k)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `degree`, `coefficient`, `collect`
